// ============================================================================
// Cloudflare configuration — Cloudflare Pages
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This site is published by Cloudflare Pages, not by a Worker. Pages reads this
// file for the build output directory, which is why it must contain
// `pages_build_output_dir`. Without that key Pages reports:
//
//   "A Wrangler configuration file was found but it does not appear to be valid.
//    Did you mean to use wrangler.toml to configure Pages? If so, then make sure
//    the file is valid and contains the `pages_build_output_dir` property."
//
// WHAT PAGES DOES WITH THIS REPOSITORY
//   • Publishes everything in ./site as the website
//   • Runs ./functions/api/lead.js as the Function behind POST /api/lead
//   • Applies site/_headers, site/_redirects and site/_routes.json
//
// There is nothing to compile: the site is already HTML, CSS and JavaScript.
// The build command in the Pages dashboard must therefore be LEFT EMPTY. If it
// is set to `pnpm run build` the build fails with
// ERR_PNPM_NO_IMPORTER_MANIFEST_FOUND, because there is no package.json.
// ============================================================================
{
  "name": "systemhelp",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./site"
}
